{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli and the Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His mother was a daughter of King Baldwin II of Jerusalem and Morphia of Melitene.\n\n* **Family and Succession** *\n\nRaymond III was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. He succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. His mother was a member of the royal family of Jerusalem and was a daughter of King Baldwin II of Jerusalem and Morphia of Melitene.\n\nRaymond III married his cousin Stephanie of Milly in 1152. Stephanie was a daughter of Guy I of Milly and a member of the royal family of Jerusalem. The marriage was a strategic move by Raymond III to secure his position as Count of Tripoli and to strengthen his ties to the royal family of Jerusalem.\n\n* **Participation in the Crusades** *\n\nRaymond III participated in the Second Crusade in 1147. He joined King Louis VII of France and King Conrad III of Germany in their campaign to retake the city of Edessa from the Muslim forces. Raymond III played a key role in the siege of the city of Edessa but was unable to retake the city.\n\nRaymond III also participated in the Crusade of 1163. He joined King Amalric I of Jerusalem and the Byzantine Emperor Manuel I Comnenus in their campaign to retake the city of Antioch from the Muslim forces. However the Crusade was unsuccessful and the city of Antioch remained in Muslim hands.\n\n* **Later Life and Death** *\n\nRaymond III died in 1187 without an heir. He was succeeded as Count of Tripoli by his nephew Bohemond IV of Antioch who was a member of the House of Antioch. Bohemond IV was the son of Raymond III's sister Hodierna of Tripoli and Bohemond III of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token":